@@@ meta
id: ARR-M-01
topic: Arrays
difficulty: Medium
type: FUNCTION
title: Maximum Subarray Sum With Its Bounds (Kadane)
tags: kadane, dynamic-programming, int64, tie-breaking, asked-in-automotive
@@@ statement_md
Implement

```c
int64_t max_subarray(const int32_t *a, int n, int *start, int *end);
```

It returns the **largest sum of a non-empty contiguous subarray** of `a[0..n-1]` and stores that subarray's inclusive bounds in `*start` and `*end`.

- The subarray must contain at least one element. If every value is negative, the answer is the largest single element, not `0`.
- **Ties:** if several subarrays reach the maximum sum, report the one with the **smallest `start`**, and among those the **smallest `end`**.
- Values cover the full `int32_t` range and `n` can be 1 000 000, so the sum needs 64 bits. The judge runs with UBSan.
- O(n) time and O(1) extra memory. An O(n^2) scan of all subarrays is too slow.

**How it is tested.** A hidden `main()` calls your function once and prints `sum start end`. It also checks that `a[start..end]` really adds up to the returned sum. Large tests are generated by the harness from a seed.

**Input (read by the hidden harness)**
- Either: line 1 `n`, line 2 the `n` values,
- or: one line `GEN n seed mode`.

**Output**
- `sum start end`

**Example**
```
Input:
9
-2 1 -3 4 -1 2 1 -5 4

Output:
6 3 6
```
The subarray `4 -1 2 1` (indices 3..6) has sum 6.
@@@ constraints_md
- `1 <= n <= 1000000`
- `INT32_MIN <= a[i] <= INT32_MAX`
- O(n) time, O(1) extra space, the array is read-only.
@@@ starter_code
#include <stdint.h>

/* Largest sum of a non-empty contiguous subarray; bounds in *start/*end.
 * Ties: smallest start, then smallest end. */
int64_t max_subarray(const int32_t *a, int n, int *start, int *end)
{
    /* TODO */
    *start = 0;
    *end = 0;
    return a[0];
}
@@@ harness_code
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <stdint.h>

/*USER_CODE*/

#define MAXN 1000000

static int32_t a[MAXN];

int main(void)
{
    char tok[16];
    int n;
    if (scanf("%15s", tok) != 1) return 0;
    if (strcmp(tok, "GEN") == 0) {
        unsigned int seed;
        int mode;
        if (scanf("%d %u %d", &n, &seed, &mode) != 3) return 0;
        if (n < 1 || n > MAXN) return 0;
        uint32_t x = seed;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            x = x * 1103515245u + 12345u;
            switch (mode) {
            case 0:  a[i] = (int32_t)((int64_t)x - 2147483648LL); break;          /* full range   */
            case 1:  a[i] = -1 - (int32_t)((x >> 4) % 1000000u); break;            /* all negative */
            case 2:  a[i] = (int32_t)((x >> 16) % 7u) - 3; break;                  /* many ties    */
            default: a[i] = (int32_t)((x >> 2) % 1250000001u) - 250000000; break;  /* large sums   */
            }
        }
    } else {
        if (sscanf(tok, "%d", &n) != 1 || n < 1 || n > MAXN) return 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
            if (scanf("%d", &a[i]) != 1) return 0;
    }

    int s = -1, e = -1;
    int64_t r = max_subarray(a, n, &s, &e);

    if (s < 0 || e < s || e >= n) {
        printf("BAD BOUNDS %d %d\n", s, e);
        return 0;
    }
    int64_t check = 0;
    for (int i = s; i <= e; i++) check += a[i];
    if (check != r) {
        printf("INCONSISTENT: returned %lld but a[%d..%d] sums to %lld\n", (long long)r, s, e, (long long)check);
        return 0;
    }
    printf("%lld %d %d\n", (long long)r, s, e);
    return 0;
}
